  "id": "COMPOUND:19889 - PROTEIN:1682",
  "verbalization": "Kurarinol is implicated in the interaction with Type-2 angiotensin II receptor through a series of molecular pathways, with the Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 28 acting as a central mediator. This protein is targeted by Kurarinol, and in turn, it is also a target of Indirubin-3'-monoxime and Plectrornatin A, all of which are linked to the Type-2 angiotensin II receptor. The evidence suggests that Kurarinol may exert its effects via a common pathway that involves the Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 28, which is a known target of multiple compounds, including those that modulate angiotensin II signaling. The overlapping targets and the consistent presence of the Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 28 in the chain of interactions imply a potential mechanism of action that involves this protein in the regulation of the Type-2 angiotensin II receptor. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of this protein in linking Kurarinol to the angiotensin II receptor, suggesting a possible mechanism of action that is not yet fully elucidated.",
